        <Data name="county"><value>Wayne</value></Data>
      </ExtendedData>
      <styleUrl>#nrhp_site</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-83.04186145899995,42.360098678000085,0</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Elk Rapids First Methodist Episcopal Church</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>First Methodist Episcopal Church
In  the late 1850s traveling pastors began to conduct Methodist services in Elk Rapids and nearby communities. First Methodist Episcopal Church was organized in the early 1870s. Services were held in a former school and then a former courthouse. The Rev. John W. Hart, who became pastor in 1899, decided the church needed a permanent building. In 1901 the congregation purchased  architectural plans created by Benjamin D. Price and his son Max C. Price, Philadelphia architects who contracted  with the Methodist Episcopal Board of Church Extensions to design a var…</p><p>County: Antrim &middot; City: Elk Rapids</p><p>Date reported: 2024</p>]]></description>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="category"><value>Historic places (NRHP)</value></Data>
        <Data name="date_reported"><value>2024</value></Data>
        <Data name="county"><value>Antrim</value></Data>
      </ExtendedData>
