    <Placemark>
      <name>Manistee County Courthouse Fountain</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://services3.arcgis.com/Jdnp1TjADvSDxMAX/arcgis/rest/services/Historical_Markers_Public_View/FeatureServer/0/1804/attachments/2032" width="320"/><br/><p>Manistee Courthouse Fountain
&lt;div&gt;This is one of two cast-iron fountains installed in front of the Manistee County Courthouse in July 1887. Jonathan Moore and William Wilkinson of Brooklyn, New York, created the design. &amp;nbsp;The fountains cost about $500 each. After a fire destroyed the courthouse in 1950, the Portage Lake Garden Club acquired this fountain and moved it to Onekama. Listed in the National Register of Historic Places, it is one of the few surviving nineteenth-century cast-iron courthouse fountains in Michigan.&lt;/div&gt;

Onekama Memorial Fountain
&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=1&gt;This fountain on…</p><p>County: Manistee &middot; City: Onekama</p><p><a href="https://catalog.archives.gov/id/25340029">More information</a></p><p>Date reported: 2012</p>]]></description>
