    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Guardian Angels Church</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://services3.arcgis.com/Jdnp1TjADvSDxMAX/arcgis/rest/services/Historical_Markers_Public_View/FeatureServer/0/1821/attachments/2075" width="320"/><br/><p>Guardian Angels Church
On January 24, 1888, a predominantly Irish and German group left St. Mary’s Catholic Church in Manistee and founded a new church. The Reverend H. W. Grimme became the church’s pastor in May 1888 and proposed that the new church be dedicated to the “Guardian Angel.” In June 1888 the congregation purchased the orchard of the Englemann homestead. There they laid the building’s cornerstone on September 2, 1888. Bishop H. J. Richter dedicated Guardian Angels Church on December 21, 1890. At 170 feet tall and topped with a 12-foot white cross, the church’s steeple placed it am…</p><p>County: Manistee &middot; City: Manistee</p><p>Date reported: 2024</p>]]></description>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="category"><value>Historic places (NRHP)</value></Data>
