    <Placemark>
      <name>Saginaw News Building</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://services3.arcgis.com/Jdnp1TjADvSDxMAX/arcgis/rest/services/Historical_Markers_Public_View/FeatureServer/0/1835/attachments/2115" width="320"/><br/><p>Saginaw News Building
In 1918 a group of investors, led by George G. and Ralph H. Booth of Booth Newspapers, met and merged the Saginaw Evening News and the Courier-Herald into the Saginaw News Courier. The paper was renamed the Saginaw Daily News in 1927 and the Saginaw News on July 24, 1936. By the mid-1950s the company had outgrown its building at the corner of Federal and South Washington Avenues. Work began on this building, adjacent to the old structure, on August 19, 1958. The new headquarters was occupied by 1960, at which time the old building was demolished. The new structure housed…</p><p>County: Saginaw &middot; City: Saginaw</p><p>Date reported: 2024</p>]]></description>
